ready: 1
kind: module
id: recall
name: Recall
summary: >-
  Brings memory back into the agent's context through load, search, cues, gut checks, checkpoints,
  and feedback.
notes: >-
  It also answers questions about what happened when, keeps always-loaded boot settings, and
  maintains the search index. When the daemon is down, the Python package and the command line
  read the stack directly and read-only.
runs_in:
  - sys.daemon
  - sys.python
  - sys.cli
owns:
  - checkpoint (DATA-CHECKPOINT)
  - boot settings
  - recall log (DATA-RECALL-LOG)
  - recall usage counts
  - search index (DATA-SEARCH-INDEX)
invariants:
  - Relevance decides whether a memory appears; salience, strength and usage decide its order.
  - Every injected memory is rendered as data with its kind, trust tier and date, never as an instruction.
  - Appearing in a load, index or cue is not use; only an agent opening, being warned by, or reporting on a memory is.
  - The search index never holds content of a purged memory after the purge returns.
  - Recall never blocks or delays the agent beyond the hook deadline, except a gut-check speed bump.
rationale: >-
  Recall is where the stratified model pays off. Ranking by salience and strength
  makes emotion and use change what the agent sees, which is the point of
  appraising experience at all. Rendering memory as labeled notes keeps whatever
  got into memory from steering the agent as an order. Counting only real use
  keeps idle memories fading on schedule instead of refreshing themselves every
  session.
